We consider the Diophantine equation
\begin{equation*}
y^{2}=(36n^{3}-19-12mn)^{2}-(2m)^{3}.
\end{equation*}

The trivial family is
\begin{equation*}
m=0,\qquad y=\pm(36n^{3}-19).
\end{equation*}

All solutions listed below are nontrivial, since \(m\neq 0\).
Each row represents two signed solutions \((n,m,\pm|y|)\), so the table gives
\(35\) nontrivial \((n,m,|y|)\)-triples, i.e.\ \(70\) signed nontrivial integer
solutions. Rows marked \(\star\) are new relative to the original
\(29\)-row table.

