\section*{Verification note}

Each row was checked by exact (arbitrary-precision) substitution into
\begin{equation*}
y^{2}=(36n^{3}-19-12mn)^{2}-(2m)^{3}.
\end{equation*}
For every listed row, both signs \(y=|y|\) and \(y=-|y|\) give valid integer
solutions because the equation only contains \(y^{2}\).

\section*{Method and completeness}

Write \(A=36n^{3}-19-12mn\), so the equation reads \(A^{2}-y^{2}=8m^{3}\).
Setting \(A=d+e\), \(y=d-e\) gives
\begin{equation*}
de=2m^{3}.
\end{equation*}
Every solution with given \(m\neq 0\) therefore arises from a signed divisor
pair \((d,e)\) of \(2m^{3}\): the pair determines \(A=d+e\), and \(n\) must be
an integer root of
\begin{equation*}
36n^{3}-12mn-(A+19)=0,
\end{equation*}
which forces \(A\equiv 5\pmod{12}\). Enumerating all divisor pairs of
\(2m^{3}\) for every \(m\) in a range and testing the resulting cubics exactly
finds \emph{all} integer solutions with \(|m|\) in that range and \(n\)
unbounded, complementing fixed-\(n\) elliptic-curve searches.

\begin{proposition}
Table~\ref{tab:quartic_integer_solutions} contains every nontrivial integer
solution of \(y^{2}=(36n^{3}-19-12mn)^{2}-(2m)^{3}\) with
\(1\le|m|\le 10^{8}\); these are the \(32\) rows other than rows \(27\),
\(31\), \(33\), whose \(|m|\) values
(\(5.38\times10^{12}\), \(2.13\times10^{8}\), \(5.26\times10^{8}\)) lie outside
the exhaustively searched window.
\end{proposition}

\section*{Mordell--Weil data for small fibers}

For fixed \(n\), with \(X=-2m\), \(Y=y\), \(c=36n^{3}-19\), the equation is the
elliptic curve
\begin{equation*}
E_{n}:\quad Y^{2}=X^{3}+36n^{2}X^{2}+12ncX+c^{2}.
\end{equation*}
Two-descent (\texttt{ellrank}, PARI/GP 2.15.4) gives exact ranks
\begin{equation*}
\operatorname{rk}E_{1}=\operatorname{rk}E_{15}
=\operatorname{rk}E_{114}=\operatorname{rk}E_{131}=1,\qquad
\operatorname{rk}E_{-4}=\operatorname{rk}E_{46}=\operatorname{rk}E_{-54}
=\operatorname{rk}E_{-57}=\operatorname{rk}E_{75}=2,
\end{equation*}
and, notably,
\begin{equation*}
\operatorname{rk}E_{19}=3,
\end{equation*}
with generators of \(X\)-coordinate \(2394\), \(7703436/1369\),
\(2123383/2601\). For \(E_{-29}\) the rank lies in \([1,3]\) and for
\(E_{93}\) in \([1,2]\) (the lower bounds from the known points).

\begin{remark}
Enumerating all \(\mathbb{Z}\)-linear combinations of the computed generators
(coefficients up to \(\pm 14\) in rank \(1\), \(\pm 7\) in rank \(2\),
\(\pm 4\) in rank \(3\), plus torsion) produced no integral even-\(X\) points
beyond those already in the table. In particular, on the rank-\(3\) fiber
\(E_{19}\), rows \(18\)--\(19\) are the only such points in that combination
range.
\end{remark}

